From ce6af424b46ed2852a58f535f3a12d2648d1fee3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 03:04:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] borg: count a Rod of Teleport Other in BI_ATPORTOTHER

The Teleport Other availability trait was filled only from a carried
Wand of Teleport Other (its charges) and from the Teleport Other spell.
A Rod of Teleport Other added nothing, so borg_power() did not rise for
it and the shop step never bought one: a Warrior with enough gold left
the rod in the Black Market.

Count each carried rod as one, like one wand charge. A Borg that already
has the spell or a full stack of wand charges values it as before.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#560.

(cherry picked from commit fc444ab17e8dee8ccdbb908f4e3bb760114089b8)
---
 src/borg/borg-trait.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-trait.c b/src/borg/borg-trait.c
index 48ffab3a2..a4939edeb 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-trait.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-trait.c
@@ -2420,6 +2420,9 @@ static void borg_notice_inventory(void)
                 } else {
                     borg.trait[BI_ASPEED] += item->iqty;
                 }
+            } else if (item->sval == sv_rod_teleport_other) {
+                /* Counted like a wand of teleport other */
+                borg.trait[BI_ATPORTOTHER] += item->iqty;
             } else if (item->sval == sv_rod_mapping)
                 borg.trait[BI_AMAGICMAP] += item->iqty * 100;
             else if (item->sval == sv_rod_healing) {
-- 
